{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"###The strategy\n\nLet's write $64$ in base $4$. Then, using the properties of exponents, we can express the entire left hand side of the equation as $4$ raised to some linear function. Finally, we can equate the exponents of the  resulting equation  to solve for the unknown.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"###Simplifying the left hand side\n\n$\\begin{align}\\dfrac{64\\^{\\Large 7x-1}}{4\\^{\\Large 2x+3}}\u0026=\\dfrac{(4^3)\\^{\\Large 7x-1}}{4\\^{\\Large 2x+3}}\u0026\u0026\u0026\u0026(64=4^3) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n \u0026=\\dfrac{4\\^{\\Large \\purpleC{21x-3}}}{4\\^{\\Large \\goldD{2x+3}}} \u0026\u0026\u0026\u0026((a^n)^m=a^{n\\cdot m})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n \u0026=4\\^{\\Large \\purpleC{21x-3} \\ - \\ (\\goldD{2x+3})}\u0026\u0026\u0026\u0026(\\dfrac{a^n}{a^m}=a^{n-m})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=4\\^{\\Large 19x-6} \\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"###Solving the equation\n\nWe obtain the following equation.\n\n$ 4\\^{\\Large 19x-6}=4\\^{\\Large 9x-4}$\n\nNow we can equate the exponents and solve for $x$.\n\n$\\begin{align}\n19x-6 \u0026=9x-4\\\\\\\\\nx \u0026= \\dfrac{1}{5}\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 2]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 2":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}19x-6 \u0026=9x-4\\\\\\\\\n10x\u0026=2\\\\\\\\\nx\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{5}\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show me more detailed steps","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"###The answer###\n\nThe answer is $x=\\dfrac{1}{5}$.\n\n*You can check this answer by substituting $\\it{x=\\dfrac{1}{5}}$ in the original equation and evaluating both sides.*","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Solve the exponential equation for $x$**.\n\n###$\\dfrac{64\\^{\\Large 7x-1}}{4\\^{\\Large 2x+3}}=4\\^{\\Large 9x-4}$\n\n$x=$ [[☃ numeric-input 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"numeric-input 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answers":[{"maxError":null,"message":"","simplify":"required","status":"correct","strict":false,"value":0.2}],"coefficient":false,"labelText":"","multipleNumberInput":false,"rightAlign":false,"size":"normal","static":false},"static":false,"type":"numeric-input","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
